  "query_preview": "..\nThe edge of a large monsoon surge is expected to bring scattered\nshowers and isolated thunderstorms later tonight through tomorrow. \nBy Sunday night, 92W looks to shift slightly closer, causing a \ndecrease in winds and sufficient moisture and instability for \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to remain. If winds \nremain light enough and cloud cover isn't too high, the light winds \nmay allow for island effect precipitation over Saipan Monday, and \nthen Guam, Tinian, and Saipan Tuesday. By Wednesday, northeasterly \nwinds will likely prevent furthur island effect as 92W moves into the\narea. As of now, most models agree that Invest 92W will move through\nas only a weak disturbance, or possibly a tropical depression, with \nonly the GFS deterministic model showing a stronger system. \nTherefore, it looks like a wetter pattern is in store for the \nMarianas by the end of next week. Invest 92W will continue to be \nmonitored closely for any changes to expected development.",
